</table>

<h2>6. Operational Questions (OQ-01 to OQ-10)</h2>
<p>Every operational question below maps directly to discrete columns and aggregations in the transaction database:</p>
<table>
    <tr><th>OQ ID</th><th>Operational Question</th><th>Underlying Data Fields</th><th>Target Metric / Output</th><th>Data Feasibility</th></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-01</strong></td><td>What is the net monthly cash flow trend (Total Credits/Inflows vs. Total Debits/Outflows)?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Transaction_Date, Transaction_Type, Amount</span></td><td>Monthly Net Cash Flow = &Sigma;(Credits) - &Sigma;(Debits)</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-02</strong></td><td>Which expense categories (Cloud, Travel, Payroll, SaaS, Hardware) drive the highest debit spending volume?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Category, Transaction_Type, Amount</span></td><td>Category-wise Total Debit Volume & % Contribution</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-03</strong></td><td>What is the corporate credit card utilization percentage relative to the sanctioned credit limits?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Account_Type, Amount, Credit_Limit, Transaction_Date</span></td><td>Credit Utilization Ratio = (Current Credit Balance / Sanctioned Limit) &times; 100</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-04</strong></td><td>What are the temporal spending patterns (peak spend by day of week, week of month, and business hours)?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Transaction_Date, Transaction_Time, Amount</span></td><td>Heatmap / Bar chart of transaction volume by weekday and monthly cycle</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-05</strong></td><td>What proportion of total monthly expenditure is financed via revolving credit versus liquid bank debits?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Payment_Instrument, Amount</span></td><td>Expenditure Proportion Ratio (Credit % vs Debit %)</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-06</strong></td><td>Who are the top 10 merchants/vendors by total expenditure and transaction count across both payment modes?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Merchant_Name, Amount, Transaction_ID, Payment_Instrument</span></td><td>Ranked table & bar chart of top 10 vendors with spend and frequency</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-07</strong></td><td>Are there anomalous transactions or statistical outliers (spending exceeding 3 standard deviations above category average)?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Transaction_ID, Category, Amount, Mean, StdDev</span></td><td>Z-Score > 3.0 / IQR Anomaly Flagged Records Table</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-08</strong></td><td>How is transaction volume distributed across payment channels (UPI, Net Banking, POS, Credit Card Gateway, NEFT)?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Payment_Channel, Transaction_ID, Amount, Status</span></td><td>Payment Channel Distribution (Count & Value Share)</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-09</strong></td><td>What is the transaction failure/decline rate across channels, and what are the primary decline reasons?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Status, Failure_Reason, Payment_Channel</span></td><td>Failure Rate % = (Failed Count / Total Count) &times; 100, broken by reason</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>OQ-10</strong></td><td>What is the Month-over-Month (MoM) expenditure growth rate across departmental cost centers?</td><td><span class='code-inline'>Department, Transaction_Date, Amount</span></td><td>MoM % Change = [(Spend_t - Spend_{t-1}) / Spend_{t-1}] &times; 100</td><td>100% Feasible</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>7. SMART Project Objectives</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>OBJ-01 (Specific & Measurable):</strong> Reduce monthly transaction reconciliation and report generation latency from 7 business days to under 5 seconds through automated SQLite database ingestion and pre-indexed analytical queries.</li>
    <li><strong>OBJ-02 (Specific & Achievable):</strong> Deliver automated classification and interactive visual exploration for 100% of corporate credit and debit transactions across 8 core expense categories.</li>
    <li><strong>OBJ-03 (Measurable & Time-bound):</strong> Implement statistical outlier detection to flag 100% of transactions exceeding 3 standard deviations from their category mean within the interactive dashboard.</li>
    <li><strong>OBJ-04 (Realistic & Performance-focused):</strong> Architect a responsive Streamlit dashboard capable of executing multi-dimensional filter queries across 50,000+ transaction records in under 1.2 seconds.</li>
    <li><strong>OBJ-05 (Relevant & Strategic):</strong> Calculate and visualize vital financial health indicators (Net Cash Flow, Credit Utilization %, Debit-to-Credit Ratio, Channel Failure Rate) with 100% computational accuracy.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Scope Definition</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th style='width: 50%;'>In-Scope (Delivered in this Project)</th><th style='width: 50%;'>Out-of-Scope (Future Enhancements)</th></tr>
    <tr>
        <td>
            <ul>
                <li>Ingestion, normalization, and relational storage of 50,000+ synthetic corporate credit and debit transactions in SQLite.</li>
                <li>Dynamic KPI cards: Total Debit Outflow, Total Credit Spend, Net Cash Flow, Active Credit Utilization %, Outlier Count.</li>
                <li>Comprehensive Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) module with Plotly visual charts (donut charts, trend lines, bar charts, boxplots).</li>
                <li>Comparative analysis of Credit vs. Debit spending volume, category breakdown, and merchant ranking.</li>
                <li>Temporal trend analysis (daily, weekly, day-of-week, and MoM variations).</li>
                <li>Statistical anomaly detection engine based on Z-score and IQR thresholding.</li>
                <li>Multi-criteria filtering (Date range, Transaction type, Category, Channel, Amount range) with CSV export capability.</li>
                <li>Automated unit test suite using <code>pytest</code> verifying data integrity, schema constraints, and business logic.</li>
                <li>Deployment on Streamlit Community Cloud with public URL access.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td>
            <ul>
                <li>Direct live integration with commercial banking core APIs (e.g., RBI Open Banking / Account Aggregator framework).</li>
                <li>Automated fund transfer execution, payment gateway checkouts, or real-time banking wire clearing.</li>
                <li>Multi-currency foreign exchange (Forex) real-time arbitrage and hedging models.</li>
                <li>Enterprise Active Directory / SSO authentication (app will provide streamlined role simulation for evaluation).</li>
                <li>Deep learning / neural network predictive models (focus is on statistical analytics, EDA, and business intelligence).</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2>9. Assumptions and Constraints</h2>
<h3>Assumptions:</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Currency & Locale:</strong> The target enterprise operates in India, with all financial transactions denominated in Indian Rupees (INR - &#8377;).</li>
    <li><strong>Synthetic Data Authenticity:</strong> In accordance with academic guidelines and privacy regulations, transactions are synthetically generated to replicate realistic corporate banking distributions, seasonality, and anomaly rates without containing real PII.</li>
    <li><strong>Temporal Horizon:</strong> The historical dataset encompasses a 24-month operational period to support robust month-over-month (MoM) and quarterly trend analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>Account Framework:</strong> Corporate credit accounts possess pre-established credit limits, billing cycle cutoff dates, and standard fee structures.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Constraints:</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Technology Constraints:</strong> Restricted to the open-source Python ecosystem (Python 3.10+, Streamlit, Pandas, NumPy, Plotly, SQLite3, Pytest).</li>
    <li><strong>Infrastructure Constraints:</strong> Deployment is bound by Streamlit Community Cloud resource quotas (maximum 1 GB RAM, containerized Linux environment).</li>
    <li><strong>Zero Cost Budget:</strong> Built entirely using free and open-source tools without proprietary enterprise software licenses.</li>
    <li><strong>Academic Timeline:</strong> Execution strictly structured across 18 sequential milestones complying with ABES MCA Capstone Project evaluation schedules.</li>
</ul>

<h2>10. Measurable Success Criteria</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Metric Area</th><th>Success Benchmark</th><th>Verification Method</th></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Query & Filter Latency</strong></td><td>Dashboard filters update all visual components in &lt; 1.2 seconds across 50,000 rows.</td><td>Execution timing benchmarks via Python <code>time</code> module.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Mathematical Accuracy</strong></td><td>Zero variance (100% accuracy) in financial aggregations, balances, and utilization formulas.</td><td>Automated unit tests with <code>pytest</code> asserting exact match against test fixtures.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Test Coverage</strong></td><td>&ge; 90% code coverage across data ingestion, calculation, and anomaly detection modules.</td><td>Pytest test execution report and coverage metrics.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Data Integrity</strong></td><td>Zero null values in primary keys; foreign key constraints strictly enforced in SQLite schema.</td><td>Schema validation queries and automated ingest assertions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>User Accessibility</strong></td><td>Zero deployment crash; public Streamlit Community Cloud URL accessible on modern web browsers.</td><td>Live cloud deployment verification and cross-browser testing.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Academic Evaluation</strong></td><td>100% compliance with ABES project guidelines, full bidirectional traceability, and defensible viva presentation.</td><td>Formal review and sign-off by Academic Mentor (Prof. Shilpa Tyagi).</td></tr>
</table>

